{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the points where the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=12$ intersects the line $x=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-8006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-4,$ we substitute $x=-4$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ (-4)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ 16-{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =12-16 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =-4 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=-4$  at the points $(-4,\\pm 2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-8006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce2e4bb2ba352af617b4f6555fa31a21236b223839a0cb8256fa40d1cf64d5e8"} {"question" "q-8006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-8006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-4,\\pm 1)"] ["math" "(-4,\\pm 2)"] ["math" "(-4,\\pm 3)"] ["math" "(-4,\\pm 4)"] ["math" "(-4,\\pm \\sqrt{12})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-8006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-4,\\pm 2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-84056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $14{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}=50$ intersects the line $y=2x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-84056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=2x,$ we first replace $y$ with $2x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2} & =50 \\\\ 14{x}^{2}-3(2x)^{2} & =50 \\\\ 14{x}^{2}-12{x}^{2} & =50 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =50 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ x & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-84056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce2e4bb2ba352af617b4f6555fa31a21236b223839a0cb8256fa40d1cf64d5e8"} {"question" "q-84056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-84056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\pm 2"] ["math" "x=\\pm 5"] ["math" "x=\\pm 5\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-84056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm 5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-170559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $5{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}=36$ intersects the line $y=-2x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-170559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-2x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-2x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 5(-2x)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 5(4{x}^{2})-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9 \\\\ x & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-170559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce2e4bb2ba352af617b4f6555fa31a21236b223839a0cb8256fa40d1cf64d5e8"} {"question" "q-170559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-170559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\pm 3"] ["math" "x=\\pm 4"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}"] ["text" "There are no points of intersection"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-170559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\pm 3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-278363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "From **top to bottom,** the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $6{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2}=30$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-278363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =30 \\\\ 6{y}^{2}-5(0)^{2} & =30 \\\\ 6{y}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =5 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,-\\sqrt{5}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-278363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ce2e4bb2ba352af617b4f6555fa31a21236b223839a0cb8256fa40d1cf64d5e8"} {"question" "q-278363" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069085/state.json" "file_sha256" "77cc6c4ac9399b9296d2b1e76b791951bc46ef846c7c14f3641854b754317ce8"} {"question" "q-278363" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivari